A||||12||MooCow||Leaking Exhuast||||5||
Z||000000||MooCow||12-11-1999||12:13 PM||||How much would it be to repaire a leak in the exhuat system on an 86Se v6 loaded?  At a dealer this guy wants now only $2,000 for the 86Se.  How much extra am I paying to get the exhuast fixed?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Linx||12-12-1999||12:09 AM||||Where's the leak? Did the dealer show you?<P>The Fiero store has most all of the exhaust in stock.  Have a look for yourself.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com/</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by Linx (edited 12-12-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||12-12-1999||12:22 AM||||Do you know where the leak is?  This will help with a estimate on the price of the repair. I think the R&R time on each manifold is 2.5hr &gt; 5hrs times shops hourly rate, with no broken bolts??? If it is a manifold crack it can be fixed. New mainifolds about 200.00ea<BR>Port and re-weld old manifolds 50.00ea. These prices are just estimates? but this should give you good idea of a price. Hope this helps.  Read some of the old post on exhaust.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||12-12-1999||03:48 AM||||How about just leave it the way it is and enjoy the buzz?  Just a thought.  Kids, don't try this at home.||||reg||1
Z||000004||stsmithgt||12-13-1999||02:39 PM||||IF the leak is your manifold nearest the firewall, I just had mine done.  The third try they finally got it right!  They originally charged me $383.22 dollars.  Due to the failure they gave a half assed second attemped.  The third time they ordered the recall kit, which cost the same as the manifold by itself.  It came with everything,(manifold, bolts, sheetmetal, gaskets, and some big tube they didn't know what to do with) They never showed me the tube.  They just told me about it.  The kit costs about 170.00 to 230.00 depending on what kind of deal they want to give you.  SOooo it came to about 600.00 and a big headache, but it sounds cool now.  I didn't have any mods done to the system. Good luck<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||12-13-1999||02:41 PM||||OOPS!  OH yeah.  Mine is an 86 4spd GT||||reg||10
Z||000006||DJRice||12-14-1999||09:41 AM||||If its a cracked manifold, then get the VIN and take it to a Pontiac Dealer and have them give you a recall history.  If the recall hasnt been done, then you are in the house.<P>If they dont want to check the recall history or dont want to take care of the work, a call to 1-800-PMCARES will solve the prob.  If recall work has not been done then they have to fix it for you.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-14-1999||11:31 AM||||Is there a time limit on the recalls?  Just wondering because I have a couple of recalls on mine that haven't been done, but I have almost 100,000miles on it.  I think one of them has to do with the engine.  Could a new, free engine be in my future??  That would be nice since mine doesn't run well now.||||reg||5
Z||000008||theogre||12-14-1999||06:25 PM||||Recalls do not expire.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||12-14-1999||11:23 PM||||Great!  Now maybe I can get a brand new motor for free.  Merry Christmas to me <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Bugsy||12-15-1999||08:57 AM||||I also have an 86 SE loaded...I bought it with an exhaust tick...had the exhaust including the converter replaced the day after i bought it...still has an exhaust tick...my fiero specialist has discovered that i have broken manifold bolts and quoted me $600 to pull the motor drill out the bolts and reinstall the motor.. I'm not sure at this point where the money is gonna come from so I'm just dealing with it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000011||Carrolles||12-15-1999||09:04 AM||||Mine had 109000 miles on it when I got it.  The parking brake recall had not been done yet.  I got a complete free brake job out of the deal.<P>Ogre's right.  Recalls don't expire.||||reg||1
Z||000012||william_thorniii||12-15-1999||06:08 PM||||Although recall's do not expire, the dealer is not required to complete them after 10 years from the issue date according to the NHTSA.  I like all of you thought that a recall = free work and parts indefinitely.   Recently, another Fiero owner made me aware of complaints to the NHTSA about recall work not being done complimentary.  I encourage any of you to try and let everyone know what you find out. <P>William T. Thorn, III<P>Good luck Monkey...||||reg||1
